es-rgds-battery-charging: the status bar's battery fills in steps while it charges, and the status bar in colour

The rnds engine draws its own battery in the status bar (the theme hides ES's batteryIndicator), and it showed the
level only: a handheld on its charger looked the same as one on battery. Themes for other frontends (Art Book Next,
TechDweeb) swap in a static charging picture (ES's batteryIndicator <incharge>, a battery with a lightning bolt).

On a charger the bar now fills to full in 4 steps of 600 ms and starts over, like the look's other stepped
animations (the bob, the meter's stripes, the cover's shine): from a quarter, or from the level when it is lower.
A first version climbed from the current level, which moved less than a pixel near full, where a handheld spends
most of its time on the charger; the level stays in the percentage ("icon and text"). A battery that is (nearly)
full holds still: ES counts a full battery on the charger as charging too (any status but "Not charging" and
"Discharging"). The charging state comes from ES's BatteryLevelWatcher through a new Source virtual (the default:
not charging), and nextWake() wakes the power saver for each step only while it charges, so a menu on battery draws
no more than before. The steps run with STILL TOP SCREEN on too: they are the only sign of charging.

The status bar is in colour too: the charging fill green (full and still included, so a battery that is plugged in
and charged reads as such), a low battery's fill (15% or less, not charging) red, and a connected Wi-Fi green. A
disconnected Wi-Fi stays the dimmed ink, since Wi-Fi is often off on purpose. The green is a new palette colour,
`ok` (#5fd068 dark, #2e9a44 light); the red is the palette's own. COLOURED STATUS ICONS (RndsStatusColors, on by
default), next to SHOW BATTERY STATUS for the ROCKNIXDS Pixel themes, turns the colours off; the steps stay.

On a charger a pixel bolt also crosses the battery (8 x 11 CSS px, centred on the 22 px body): the ink, outlined by
1 px of the screen's background, so it reads over the green fill, the empty bar and a fill in the ink alike.

